.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt OTELCONF 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm otelconf
.Nd validate and query the system OpenTelemetry configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm check
.Op Fl eq
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm show
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm get
.Ar key
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar defaults
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Cm fluentbit
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads
.Xr otel.conf 5
with the same code and checks that the base exporter library uses, so
a configuration it accepts is accepted by every telemetry program.
.Pp
The global options select other files than
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
.Pq Fl d
and
.Pa /etc/otel.conf
.Pq Fl f .
A path that does not exist contributes nothing.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "fluentbit"
.It Cm check Op Fl eq
Load and validate both files, the exporter credentials file and the
agent credentials file.
Prints
.Dq otel.conf: OK
unless
.Fl q
is given; errors are always reported.
With
.Fl e ,
also fail with exit status 3 when
.Ic enable
is false; the rc.d services use this.
.It Cm show
Print every resolved setting.
Header values are redacted.
.It Cm get Ar key
Print one resolved setting.
.Ar key
is a key of
.Xr otel.conf 5
written with dots, such as
.Cm endpoint ,
.Cm spool.directory
or
.Cm agent.upstream ;
.Cm agent.listen.host
and
.Cm agent.listen.port
print the parts of
.Ic agent.listen .
List-valued keys
.Pq Cm resource , Cm agent.tail
print one entry per line.
.It Cm fluentbit Op Fl o Ar output Op Fl u Ar user
Render the YAML configuration of the local agent,
.Xr fluent-bit 8 :
an OTLP/HTTP input on
.Ic agent.listen ,
a tail input for
.Ic agent.tail ,
filesystem buffering under
.Ic spool.directory
bounded by
.Ic spool.max_bytes ,
and an OpenTelemetry output to
.Ic agent.upstream
carrying the agent credentials.
Fails when
.Ic agent.upstream
is empty.
Without
.Fl o
the configuration is written to standard output.
With
.Fl o ,
it is written to a new mode 0600 file in the directory of
.Ar output ,
synchronized, and renamed over
.Ar output ;
.Fl u
gives that file to
.Ar user
first.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Usage errors and unknown keys exit 2; a disabled configuration exits 3
for
.Cm check Fl e
and
.Cm fluentbit .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ otelconf check
otel.conf: OK
$ otelconf get endpoint
http://localhost:4318
# otelconf fluentbit -o /var/run/otel/fluent-bit.yaml -u _otel
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr oe_sysconf 3 ,
.Xr otel.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
.Sh CAVEATS
The Fluent Bit property names follow the Fluent Bit 5.1 documentation;
they are exercised against the agent only once it is part of the base
system.
